<title>USA: Houston Ship Channel open, ice slows traffic.</title>
<headline>Houston Ship Channel open, ice slows traffic.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Houston Ship Channel is open Monday morning despite icy waters generated from winter storms that have reduced water traffic substantially, a U.S. Coast Guard port official said.</p>
<p>&quot;It's real nasty out there, the tugs aren't running but once the temperatures warm a little bit they'll start boarding,&quot; the Coast Guard official said.</p>
<p>Winter storms knocked out power lines, caused icy driving conditions and left some 180,000 Houston Light and Power Co customers without electricity on Monday.</p>
<p>((--New York Energy Desk, +1 212 859 1828))</p>
